1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:07,000
In an attempt to save Mizuha, Fushi decides to take on Funa's form.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:11,000
And you thought that it worked by giving out these things?

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Because I was using the knocker. I used it and I won.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Finally, Fushi returns home to his friends.

5
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:29,000
I don't... think that anyone is really happy.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:38,000
In a lonely night, I ask for help.

7
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Can I save myself?

8
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:50,000
The voice of the heart is ringing.

9
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:56,000
The voice of the heart is ringing.

10
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:00,000
The voice of the heart is ringing.

11
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:06,000
The voice of the heart is ringing.

12
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:10,000
The voice of the heart is ringing.

13
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:16,000
The voice of the heart is ringing.

14
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:24,000
誰かが変わってくれたなら それで救われるのか

15
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:32,420
不滅のあなたへ叫びたい 夢動く代わりに歌いたい

16
00:01:32,420 --> 00:01:40,160
言葉と言葉を重ねて 秘密の彼方へ

17
00:01:46,000 --> 00:02:05,320
あなたのハウルに grandfather ティナイ

18
00:02:05,320 --> 00:02:07,880
水侙戦の未来

19
00:02:07,880 --> 00:02:12,860
置く数が探し合った

20
00:02:12,860 --> 00:02:13,700
Uh-huh.

21
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:35,240
Ow!

22
00:02:35,240 --> 00:02:36,820
Hey, Goo Goo.

23
00:02:36,820 --> 00:02:38,020
Oh, these injuries?

24
00:02:38,020 --> 00:02:40,780
I did that plastic surgery thing I heard about.

25
00:02:40,780 --> 00:02:43,180
Your mask was broken.

26
00:02:43,180 --> 00:02:45,660
Uh, I stupidly fell down some stairs.

27
00:02:45,660 --> 00:02:47,660
That's why my clothes are torn.

28
00:02:47,660 --> 00:02:49,360
Me and Hyrule fell together.

29
00:02:49,360 --> 00:02:51,120
Uh-huh.

30
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:52,300
Aw, gross.

31
00:02:52,300 --> 00:02:53,720
Are you OK?

32
00:02:53,720 --> 00:02:54,820
Did you injure your mouth?

33
00:02:54,820 --> 00:02:57,100
Your dentures must have broken when you fell down the stairs

34
00:02:57,100 --> 00:02:57,800
with me, right?

35
00:02:57,800 --> 00:03:01,460
Why won't you tell me what really happened with you guys?

36
00:03:01,460 --> 00:03:02,800
Are you all right?

37
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:05,300
Can you eat OK?

38
00:03:05,300 --> 00:03:06,500
Don't worry, Fushi.

39
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:07,940
It was just one of those days.

40
00:03:07,940 --> 00:03:10,180
Gramps and Aiko weren't home, and I was running errands,

41
00:03:10,180 --> 00:03:12,120
so things cut a little out of hand.

42
00:03:12,120 --> 00:03:13,920
Oh, ew.

43
00:03:13,920 --> 00:03:16,560
I'm just super happy you're back home with us.

44
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:18,580
Hey, I should let Bon know you're back.

45
00:03:18,580 --> 00:03:20,520
Oh, where is Bon anyway?

46
00:03:20,520 --> 00:03:23,860
He had to go overseas on some sort of business trip.

47
00:03:23,860 --> 00:03:26,500
Oh, Fushi, so you decided to come back at last.

48
00:03:26,500 --> 00:03:27,640
Masar!

49
00:03:27,640 --> 00:03:28,740
Look at everybody!

50
00:03:28,740 --> 00:03:29,960
What's happened?

51
00:03:29,960 --> 00:03:30,460
Huh?

52
00:03:30,460 --> 00:03:31,340
What are you talking about?

53
00:03:31,340 --> 00:03:32,500
There's nothing wrong with them.

54
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:33,800
No, but...

55
00:03:33,800 --> 00:03:34,640
What's the matter?

56
00:03:34,640 --> 00:03:37,680
Does it look like they've all changed since you ran away from home?

57
00:03:37,680 --> 00:03:38,680
Mm-hmm.

58
00:03:38,680 --> 00:03:42,360
They were all dragged into this new world without any warning or instruction.

59
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:44,620
Now they're trying to figure out how to live here.

60
00:03:44,620 --> 00:03:46,120
That's pretty much it.

61
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:47,120
That's it?

62
00:03:47,120 --> 00:03:48,720
That's why they're all sad?

63
00:03:48,720 --> 00:03:51,960
Well, no one's dead, and they're doing better than they did before.

64
00:03:51,960 --> 00:03:54,560
But it takes more than a new world to phase me.

65
00:03:54,560 --> 00:03:55,640
Yeah, that's true.

66
00:03:55,640 --> 00:03:57,900
You haven't changed at all, Masar.

67
00:03:57,900 --> 00:03:59,900
That's because I can see clearly.

68
00:03:59,900 --> 00:04:02,500
You should try taking a good look at your friends.

69
00:04:02,500 --> 00:04:03,800
Uh-huh.

70
00:04:14,480 --> 00:04:15,480
Hey, Gugu.

71
00:04:15,480 --> 00:04:16,380
Check it out.

72
00:04:16,380 --> 00:04:18,180
I just made a new mask for you.

73
00:04:18,180 --> 00:04:20,280
Oh, thank you.

74
00:04:20,280 --> 00:04:22,060
Sorry if it's not perfect.

75
00:04:22,060 --> 00:04:23,320
About what happened.

76
00:04:23,320 --> 00:04:26,860
I don't think it really broke after falling down some stairs.

77
00:04:26,860 --> 00:04:27,460
Ouch!

78
00:04:27,460 --> 00:04:28,460
Oh!

79
00:04:28,460 --> 00:04:30,560
It's kind of rubbing against my wound.

80
00:04:30,560 --> 00:04:31,740
Uh, sorry.

81
00:04:31,740 --> 00:04:32,740
I know.

82
00:04:32,740 --> 00:04:33,740
How about this?

83
00:04:33,740 --> 00:04:35,060
It's really fluffy.

84
00:04:35,060 --> 00:04:36,060
Ha!

85
00:04:36,060 --> 00:04:37,140
What's this weird thing?

86
00:04:37,140 --> 00:04:38,140
Huh?

87
00:04:38,140 --> 00:04:39,140
Don't you remember?

88
00:04:39,140 --> 00:04:40,780
That's the crayfish mask that Reen made for you.

89
00:04:40,780 --> 00:04:42,140
Doesn't it take you back?

90
00:04:42,140 --> 00:04:44,340
So Reen made this?

91
00:04:44,340 --> 00:04:45,340
Mm-hmm.

92
00:04:45,340 --> 00:04:49,180
But I just called it weird, and it turns out Reen made this!

93
00:04:49,180 --> 00:04:50,380
She made it for me!

94
00:04:50,380 --> 00:04:51,580
Mm-hmm.

95
00:04:51,580 --> 00:04:52,580
Oh!

96
00:04:52,580 --> 00:04:53,580
That's right.

97
00:04:53,580 --> 00:04:56,580
She never had the chance to properly give it to you.

98
00:04:56,580 --> 00:04:57,580
Hmm.

99
00:04:57,580 --> 00:04:58,580
How's it look?

100
00:04:58,580 --> 00:05:00,580
It looks real good!

101
00:05:00,580 --> 00:05:01,580
Of course.

102
00:05:01,580 --> 00:05:03,700
And Reen made it?

103
00:05:03,700 --> 00:05:04,700
Mm-hmm.

104
00:05:04,700 --> 00:05:05,700
Hmm.

105
00:05:05,700 --> 00:05:06,700
Hmm.

106
00:05:06,700 --> 00:05:08,700
I wish I could go back to Takunaha.

107
00:05:08,700 --> 00:05:09,700
Uh...

108
00:05:09,700 --> 00:05:10,700
Huh?

109
00:05:10,700 --> 00:05:11,700
Huh?

110
00:05:11,700 --> 00:05:12,700
Huh?

111
00:05:12,700 --> 00:05:13,700
But...

112
00:05:13,700 --> 00:05:14,700
Really?

113
00:05:14,700 --> 00:05:15,700
Why, though?

114
00:05:15,700 --> 00:05:16,700
You're... not... happy?

115
00:05:16,700 --> 00:05:17,700
And...

116
00:05:17,700 --> 00:05:18,700
Yaname?

117
00:05:18,700 --> 00:05:19,700
It.

118
00:05:19,700 --> 00:05:21,700
You first brought me back to life in Takunaha, right?

119
00:05:29,700 --> 00:05:32,700
Well, Boozman's shop was still there.

120
00:05:32,700 --> 00:05:36,700
And seeing it brought back some memories for me.

121
00:05:36,700 --> 00:05:37,700
Ha!

122
00:05:37,700 --> 00:05:39,700
I'm just messing.

123
00:05:39,700 --> 00:05:40,700
Night.

124
00:05:40,700 --> 00:05:41,700
Uh...

125
00:05:41,700 --> 00:05:42,700
Uh...

126
00:05:42,700 --> 00:05:59,700
Maybe this place wasn't such a good choice for all of them after all.

127
00:05:59,700 --> 00:06:00,700
Hey, Fushi!

128
00:06:00,700 --> 00:06:02,700
I just received a message from Bon.

129
00:06:02,700 --> 00:06:04,700
He says you should come check this out.

130
00:06:04,700 --> 00:06:05,700
Hmm?

131
00:06:05,700 --> 00:06:07,700
It's the International Weeding Federation.

132
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:11,700
They say they're gonna get rid of all the roots you've spread over the past 500 years.

133
00:06:11,700 --> 00:06:16,700
The troublesome roots from Renrul have stopped growing, so now's the perfect time to get rid of them and clean up.

134
00:06:16,700 --> 00:06:17,700
You're incorrect, sir.

135
00:06:17,700 --> 00:06:18,700
Oh, it's fine.

136
00:06:18,700 --> 00:06:19,700
The Great Tree is still alive.

137
00:06:19,700 --> 00:06:21,700
Another Fushi fundamentalist.

138
00:06:21,700 --> 00:06:23,700
You're just as stubborn as those roots.

139
00:06:23,700 --> 00:06:25,700
Your ideology's a curse.

140
00:06:25,700 --> 00:06:26,700
No!

141
00:06:26,700 --> 00:06:27,700
I am not a curse!

142
00:06:27,700 --> 00:06:29,700
And I'm not done yet!

143
00:06:29,700 --> 00:06:34,700
The idea that the roots have stopped growing is a lie spread by the Church of Bennett.

144
00:06:36,700 --> 00:06:37,700
No, right!

145
00:06:37,700 --> 00:06:39,700
That's right.

146
00:06:39,700 --> 00:06:40,700
I can keep going.

147
00:06:40,700 --> 00:07:04,700
Hello, welcome!

148
00:07:04,700 --> 00:07:07,700
I am at work, you know.

149
00:07:07,700 --> 00:07:11,700
I'm here to find out what happened to you and Gugu.

150
00:07:11,700 --> 00:07:12,700
I need to know.

151
00:07:12,700 --> 00:07:15,700
It's like he said, we both fell down some stairs.

152
00:07:15,700 --> 00:07:18,700
Oh, by the way, do you still have dentures?

153
00:07:18,700 --> 00:07:21,700
Yeah, I still have my old ones with me.

154
00:07:21,700 --> 00:07:23,700
Are you sure you don't want the newest ones?

155
00:07:23,700 --> 00:07:34,700
Apparently, Gugu has been struggling to fit in at school ever since the very first day.

156
00:07:34,700 --> 00:07:36,700
Why are you wearing that mask?

157
00:07:36,700 --> 00:07:37,700
I have an injury.

158
00:07:37,700 --> 00:07:38,700
Let me see!

159
00:07:38,700 --> 00:07:39,700
Come on!

160
00:07:39,700 --> 00:07:41,700
Take this mask off and show us!

161
00:07:41,700 --> 00:07:45,700
Everyone at the school was fascinated by him.

162
00:07:45,700 --> 00:07:48,700
They pestered him with their curiosity.

163
00:07:48,700 --> 00:07:52,700
It's really a shame you and I aren't in the same grade together.

164
00:07:52,700 --> 00:07:57,700
Maybe if I just show them my face, they'll be satisfied.

165
00:07:57,700 --> 00:08:00,700
Oh, you're... normal?

166
00:08:00,700 --> 00:08:03,700
Hey now, will you stop bullying the new kid?

167
00:08:03,700 --> 00:08:04,700
I'm not, sir.

168
00:08:04,700 --> 00:08:07,700
I'm just really fascinated about his strange mask.

169
00:08:07,700 --> 00:08:10,700
Unfortunately, the rumors spread, which brought even more trouble.

170
00:08:10,700 --> 00:08:11,700
What's up?

171
00:08:11,700 --> 00:08:13,700
Are you afraid to show your face?

172
00:08:13,700 --> 00:08:16,700
Don't you know that Ah-chan is in charge of this area?

173
00:08:16,700 --> 00:08:20,700
You've got some nerve wandering over here without saying hi to him.

174
00:08:20,700 --> 00:08:21,700
Who's Ah-chan?

175
00:08:21,700 --> 00:08:23,700
What'd you say to me?!

176
00:08:24,700 --> 00:08:25,700
Ouch!

177
00:08:25,700 --> 00:08:28,700
Ah-chan, this guy's bad news!

178
00:08:28,700 --> 00:08:31,700
So, you think you're a tough guy, is that right?

179
00:08:31,700 --> 00:08:33,700
Hey, no! I haven't done anything!

180
00:08:33,700 --> 00:08:36,700
Wannabe town mascot trying to take over my area!

181
00:08:38,700 --> 00:08:39,700
Hey, just leave him alone!

182
00:08:39,700 --> 00:08:40,700
What's that?

183
00:08:40,700 --> 00:08:41,700
Huh?

184
00:08:41,700 --> 00:08:42,700
You cracked it!

185
00:08:42,700 --> 00:08:45,700
Look at what you've done to my mask!

186
00:08:45,700 --> 00:08:47,700
You'll pay for that!

187
00:08:47,700 --> 00:08:48,700
You do chill out!

188
00:08:48,700 --> 00:08:50,700
You'll cause trouble for Kazumitsu!

189
00:08:50,700 --> 00:08:51,700
Take this!

190
00:08:52,700 --> 00:08:54,700
Are you kidding me?

191
00:08:54,700 --> 00:08:55,700
What the?!

192
00:08:55,700 --> 00:08:57,700
That didn't hurt!

193
00:09:02,700 --> 00:09:03,700
Alrighty then.

194
00:09:03,700 --> 00:09:05,700
I guess I'm getting mixed up in this as well.

195
00:09:05,700 --> 00:09:06,700
Thanks, man.

196
00:09:09,700 --> 00:09:10,700
No!

197
00:09:10,700 --> 00:09:11,700
No!

198
00:09:11,700 --> 00:09:12,700
No!

199
00:09:16,700 --> 00:09:18,700
That kept happening to us for days.

200
00:09:18,700 --> 00:09:22,700
Until eventually, we were detained by something called the police.

201
00:09:22,700 --> 00:09:24,700
That's pretty much everything up to yesterday.

202
00:09:24,700 --> 00:09:28,700
Gugu told me that he wanted to go back to Takunaha.

203
00:09:28,700 --> 00:09:33,700
Sure, I know that place is really nice, but then...

204
00:09:34,700 --> 00:09:37,700
Is living here really that bad?

205
00:09:37,700 --> 00:09:40,700
Honestly, I don't know.

206
00:09:40,700 --> 00:09:44,700
But either way, I'm going to be leaving that house within a year.

207
00:09:45,700 --> 00:09:46,700
But why?!

208
00:09:46,700 --> 00:09:49,700
There's a place for you to sleep and the food is good!

209
00:09:49,700 --> 00:09:51,700
I just need something else.

210
00:09:51,700 --> 00:09:53,700
I can't keep living like a kid forever.

211
00:09:53,700 --> 00:09:58,700
If you count all the years I've lived, I'm actually older than Kazumitsu.

212
00:09:58,700 --> 00:10:00,700
Well, I don't get it!

213
00:10:00,700 --> 00:10:02,700
Is this place not good enough for anyone?!

214
00:10:02,700 --> 00:10:03,700
What's wrong with it?!

215
00:10:03,700 --> 00:10:04,700
School?!

216
00:10:04,700 --> 00:10:05,700
Is it me?!

217
00:10:05,700 --> 00:10:06,700
Hey, no, calm down.

218
00:10:06,700 --> 00:10:08,700
I'm not leaving because I don't like it.

219
00:10:08,700 --> 00:10:12,700
Actually, it's because this world that you've brought us into is so much fun.

220
00:10:12,700 --> 00:10:15,700
I just want to go out there and explore some more of it.

221
00:10:21,700 --> 00:10:23,700
Hey, where are you going?!

222
00:10:23,700 --> 00:10:25,700
I can do more!

223
00:10:30,700 --> 00:10:33,700
So, you weren't kidding about going back to Takunaha?

224
00:10:33,700 --> 00:10:38,700
You seriously think Fushi's gonna send you off with a smile the way things are going right now?

225
00:10:38,700 --> 00:10:41,700
I'm sure he already knows the truth.

226
00:10:41,700 --> 00:10:45,700
I just didn't want him to see me all beat up like that after those fights.

227
00:10:45,700 --> 00:10:47,700
Man, when he come home now?

228
00:10:47,700 --> 00:10:49,700
Damn it, Fushi.

229
00:10:49,700 --> 00:10:51,700
Just tell him everything that's pissing you off.

230
00:10:51,700 --> 00:10:54,700
I don't want to be that kind of brother. No way.

231
00:10:54,700 --> 00:10:55,700
Really?

232
00:10:55,700 --> 00:10:58,700
I definitely prefer that kind of brother.

233
00:11:01,700 --> 00:11:02,700
That's what I think.

234
00:11:02,700 --> 00:11:05,700
Big brother ought to understand his little brother.

235
00:11:05,700 --> 00:11:07,700
Hey, you guys. Have you seen Fushi?

236
00:11:07,700 --> 00:11:09,700
No. He ain't here.

237
00:11:09,700 --> 00:11:13,700
I told him how he got our injuries and he ran off. Like he had an idea.

238
00:11:13,700 --> 00:11:15,700
I thought he came back to see you.

239
00:11:18,700 --> 00:11:20,700
It's only us and the animals here at the moment.

240
00:11:20,700 --> 00:11:24,700
Hey, everyone. Can any of you help me find Fushi?

241
00:11:25,700 --> 00:11:27,700
Great. Let's go.

242
00:11:28,700 --> 00:11:31,700
Hang on a minute. You mean they can understand us?

243
00:11:31,700 --> 00:11:33,700
Don't worry. I'll find him.

244
00:11:33,700 --> 00:11:36,700
I wonder if he went this way.

245
00:11:36,700 --> 00:11:38,700
Oh, no. Look, it's another fight.

246
00:11:38,700 --> 00:11:42,700
It's that masked boy again? Oh, dear.

247
00:11:42,700 --> 00:11:43,700
Hold him!

248
00:11:44,700 --> 00:11:47,700
Hey, Fushi! It's you, isn't it?

249
00:11:47,700 --> 00:11:48,700
Cut it out!

250
00:11:48,700 --> 00:11:49,700
Gugu? What are you doing here?

251
00:11:49,700 --> 00:11:50,700
Will you quit talking? Get lost!

252
00:11:50,700 --> 00:11:51,700
Run! This way!

253
00:11:51,700 --> 00:11:52,700
Get back here, asshole!

254
00:11:52,700 --> 00:11:53,700
What the hell are you doing?

255
00:11:53,700 --> 00:11:56,700
Fighting those guys in my mask.

256
00:11:56,700 --> 00:12:05,700
I'm sorry.

257
00:12:05,700 --> 00:12:09,700
Hey, I know that face. Nando. I knew it. But why did you choose him?

258
00:12:09,700 --> 00:12:12,700
Because he's the closest to you in build and muscle.

259
00:12:12,700 --> 00:12:13,700
That's your reason?

260
00:12:13,700 --> 00:12:18,700
Well, I wanted to find out how your life has been going lately. And as I was walking through town, those guys picked a fight with me.

261
00:12:19,700 --> 00:12:22,700
It's just... anyone who hurts you, I'm sorry.

262
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:23,700
What the hell are you doing?

263
00:12:23,700 --> 00:12:24,700
What the hell are you doing?

264
00:12:24,700 --> 00:12:25,700
Fighting those guys in my mask?

265
00:12:26,700 --> 00:12:27,700
I'm sorry.

266
00:12:28,700 --> 00:12:31,700
Hey, I know that face. Nando. I knew it. But why did you choose him?

267
00:12:32,700 --> 00:12:34,700
Because he's the closest to you in build and muscle.

268
00:12:35,700 --> 00:12:36,700
That's your reason?

269
00:12:36,700 --> 00:12:47,700
It's just... anyone who hurts you, hurts me. So, I got angry. I'm sorry, Gugu. It put you through so much pain, I never noticed.

270
00:12:48,700 --> 00:12:54,700
